SUMMARY:Startribe Summer Solstice Dance w/David Starfire at Pack Square 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Movement Collective\nGet tickets at http://startribe
 .org\n{This is a pre-sales only event}\n\nEssentials:\n\\- Doors 6:45pm\\.
 \n\\- Open to ages 18 and older\n\\- StarTribe is booze\\\, drug\\\, and s
 moke free\\.\n\\- StarTribe Dances are rain or shine\\!\n\\- YES\\\, this 
 event WILL sell out\\! Maximum attendance is 500\; get your ticket NOW to 
 secure your entry\\!\n\nDancing on the Summer Solstice...\n...with your Tr
 ibe...\n...in the magical setting of Pack Square Park...\n...to a LIVE set
  with David Starfire...\n...amplified by the 24 speaker StarTribe Sound Sy
 stem...\n...AWESOMENESS here we come.\n\nDavid Starfire\nHeadline for the 
 Summer Solstice Dance\, David Starfire\, is known as the pioneer of the Gl
 obal Bass genre and composer of music for meditation and psychedelic assis
 ted therapy. Billboard summed it up best: "David Starfire brings a unique 
 perspective to EDM."\nDavid's Ascend album reached #7 on the iTunes World 
 Music chart and he had two #1 remixes on Hype Machine. He's traded remixes
  with CloZee\, Desert Dwellers\, iLL Gates\, Beats Antique\, and SOOHAN.\n
 David has performed at prominent festivals such as Winter Music Conference
 \, Coachella\, Outside Lands\, Envision\, Burning Man\, Eclipse\, and Ligh
 tning in a Bottle.\n\nDJ Osiah\nAn ecstatic dancer turned DJ with a deep l
 ove for crafting ecstatic dance medicine journeys that break through the l
 imiting ideas as to what “spiritual” is supposed to look and sound lik
 e. His mixes don't play by the rules. They are deep\, bass-rich\, soul-exp
 anding\, multi-genre\, feeling-inducing meditations bringing in a full spe
 ctrum of e-motions that synchronistically match the vibe-sense context of 
 the present moment at hand.\n\nThe StarTribe Vision\nAt StarTribe\, we tre
 asure finding solace in the company of kindred spirits\, sharing love\, jo
 y\, and the magic of dance.\nIt's unanimous: StarTribe dances are where th
 e human spirit shines bright. (We don't call ourselves StarTribe for nothi
 n'!)\nTogetherness is the spirit of StarTribe\, and you are warmly invited
 .
